/*
 * NocSif — LVGL v9 UI layer. See ui.h.
 *
 * M3 established the esp_lvgl_port glue (tick/task/mutex/flush + panel-IO
 * trans-done wiring) over our CO5300 panel + CST9217 touch. UI-shell P1/P2 added
 * the embedded fonts + colour tokens (ui_theme) and the static orrery/star
 * background on lv_layer_bottom() with corner masks on lv_layer_top() (ui_background).
 *
 * UI-shell P3 (this file's current job): replace the M3/M4 demo sampler with the
 * menu-first navigation SHELL — Home -> submenu -> action screens, a screen stack
 * with a 240 ms directional slide (ui_nav), transparent screen roots so the orrery
 * shows through. P3.1 = the nav skeleton (Home + WiFi submenu + the USB action screen
 * carrying the existing M4 controls) to prove the transparent-screen slide over the
 * persistent orrery. Icons + the larger type scale land in P3.2; the rest of the
 * screen map (NFC/BLE/System submenus, the WiFi Scan action shell) in P3.3.
 *
 * Load-bearing M3 invariants kept verbatim (see the flush config below):
 *   - buffer_size is in PIXELS (port x3 for RGB888); .color_format = RGB888 (defaults
 *     to RGB565); .buff_dma = false (port rejects DMA buffers with RGB888).
 *   - the 2-px ui_rounder_cb (CO5300 needs even column/row alignment or partial
 *     flushes shear).
 *   - CONFIG_LV_COLOR_DEPTH_24=y (=y, not =24 — silently ignored otherwise).
 *
 * P3.1 render mode change (fixes the banded/hoppy nav slide): switched from partial
 * internal draw buffers to FULL-FRAME PSRAM buffers with .full_refresh. Each frame is
 * now rendered whole into a 410x502 PSRAM buffer and flushed as ONE draw_bitmap (the
 * SPI bus max_transfer_sz already chunks it, M1 precedent) instead of assembled band
 * by band — so the full-screen slide composes atomically rather than sweeping top to
 * bottom per frame. buff_spiram is required (two full frames = 1.23 MB won't fit
 * internal RAM; ~7.6 MB PSRAM free) and frees ~98 KB internal RAM. full_refresh only
 * renders/flushes when something invalidates, so an idle Home still never repaints
 * (P2 property preserved); a periodic widget (P4 clock) costs one full flush per tick.
 */
